    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d852">

                <pb facs="0989" n="877" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg877"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894.6363/163: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-01-04T18:00:00-05:00">January 4, 1935—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2. Your 1, January 4, 5 p.m. Department is inclined to the opinion that British
                    and American oil interests should use every opportunity to impress upon the
                    Japanese Government the fact that they are in complete accord and that they are
                    in this case acting unitedly. Department therefore believes that the special
                    representatives of the American and British oil interests should endeavor to
                    arrange for joint conferences with the Japanese authorities.</p>
                <pb facs="0990" n="878" xml:id="pg878"/>
                <p>If you concur, you may inform the American oil interests in the sense of the
                    foregoing, emphasizing, however, that decision in regard to this matter rests
                    with the oil interests and not with the American Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
